# enum_discriminant_constant_expressions - an enum variant's discriminant is a compile-time integer expression: shifts, an OR of the enum's own variants, a named constant, a forward reference, a negative value; a variant without one takes the one after its predecessor's, and the folded tags reach a cast, a match and an array size.
